{"step_index":1700,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:51:48Z","input_tokens":3180,"cache_read_tokens":221026,"output_tokens":2546,"thinking":"The initial message indicating a testnet environment needs updating to reflect a real-time trading environment with micro-capital. Replacing the existing message with new details about the live connection and available funds addresses this. Subsequently, adding a live position ticker effect near the trade execution step will enhance real-time information.\n\n\nA manual market close event is being processed, capturing the final profit/loss (P&L), updating the balance, and recording key information. The current balance is updated, and peak balance is tracked if it exceeds the previous high. Trade count is incremented.\n\nBased on whether the trade resulted in a win or loss, the number of consecutive losses is reset/incremented, and the agent's internal evolution is updated with experience points and adjusted weights based on the outcome. A new log entry documenting the market close details is added, and the chart history is updated with the new balance.\n\n\nManual position closure triggered; the current live position is being cleared from state, and a descriptive log message is being generated with the final P&L and new bankroll amount. A calculation determining real-time P&L is initiated, dependent on Bybit's live price feeds and the position's characteristics. The take-profit/stop-loss condition is evaluated by comparing the current live price to the predetermined target prices for the active position.\n\n\nThe balance is updated with the final P&L, recording the new value and checking for a new peak. The total number of trades is incremented.\n\nBased on the trade's outcome, consecutive losses are managed, experience points are added, and the evolution of the agent's weights is adjusted. A new log entry provides detailed information about the trade's result, including P&L, percentage gain/loss, and a descriptive message. The chart history is updated with a new entry containing the current balance.\n\n\nPosition closure is now confirmed with live data, recording the outcome and updating the current bankroll. The active position's details are cleared to prevent further real-time calculations on a closed trade.\n\nA new position is considered if the imbalance in the order book depth exceeds a threshold and news is clear, initiating a buy or sell order based on the imbalance direction. The BTCUSDT ticker's last price is used as the current price to determine the notional USD and margin used.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"/Users/dev/Documents/Antigravity/grok-bot-dashboard/src/engine/useTradingSimulation.ts","EndLine":230,"StartLine":200,"toolAction":"Viewing useTradingSimulation lines 200-230","toolSummary":"View lines 200-230"}}]}
